  "body": "### Context\nPR #372 (branch `legacy/duo-inner-cover`, base `master`) puts the iPad split view on the unfolded iPhone Duo and keeps the tab bar on the cover screen. It was written in a Linux container with no Xcode: **nothing has been built**. This issue holds the checks for a Mac.\n\n### 1. Build\n```sh\ngit fetch origin legacy/duo-inner-cover && git checkout legacy/duo-inner-cover\nset -o pipefail\nxcodebuild -project SuperHFRplus.xcodeproj -scheme HFRswift -configuration Debug -destination 'generic/platform=iOS Simulator' build 2>&1 | grep -E \"error:|warning: .*(MainWindow|Common|MessagesView)\\.swift|BUILD SUCCEEDED|BUILD FAILED\"\n```\nExpected: `BUILD SUCCEEDED`, with no new warnings in `MainWindow.swift`, `Common.swift` or `MessagesView.swift`. If SwiftLint is installed, run `swiftlint` on these files: 0 new warnings.\n\n### 2. Simulator or device: iPhone Duo **open**, portrait then landscape\nLaunch the app with Console filtered on `[RootTabAudit]`.\n- [x] The root is the split view: sidebar (Forum / Outils / Plus) + list + topic. There is no tab bar. The log shows `mode=sidebar`.\n- [x] Catégories → category → topic: the topic opens in the right panel. « Masquer la liste » works.\n- [x] Favoris, Messages, Bookmarks, Alertes Qualitay → topic: each opens in the detail.\n- [ ] Réglages / Recherche: two-column split, no empty panel.\n- [x] Rotation portrait ↔ landscape: the split view stays. The app is never upside down.\n- [x] Navigation titles are compact (inline). Scroll a long list, then push a topic: **no hang** (iOS 27.1 workaround).\n- [ ] Refresh button: the icon spins, no giant white bubble.\n- [x] Animated GIFs in a topic are sharp (not 3× too large or blurry).\n- [x] Long press on a message → the edit menu is anchored inside the detail column.\n- [x] Portrait width of the detail: readable? (screenshot)\n\n### 3. iPhone Duo **closed** (cover screen)\n- [ ] Tab bar, content edge to edge, **no black bands or letterboxing**, safe areas respected (screenshot).\n- [ ] Larger Dynamic Type (Settings › Accessibility › AX3): lists and topic stay readable, nothing is cut off.\n- [x] « Rotation d'écran » set to Non: portrait lock in place. Set to Oui: landscape works.\n\n### 4. Fold / unfold\n- [x] **Reading**: open a topic on page 3, then unfold. Note what you see (expected and known: the topic is not carried over, the split shows its empty detail). Same test the other way. No crash, no frozen screen.\n- [ ] **Writing**: open the reply composer, type text, fold then unfold. The composer stays usable, closing it keeps the draft (reopen with `+`). Post, and check whether the topic refreshes (known risk: it does not after a fold).\n- [ ] Fold while in landscape with the composer open: the cover screen goes back to portrait.\n- [ ] Log: `splitVisibility.sizeClassChanged` / `verticalSizeClassChanged` appear, with no repeated loop of `rootMode` changes during the animation.\n\n### 5. Non-regression\n- [ ] iPad (full screen, Split View, Stage Manager): same behaviour as `master`.\n- [ ] iPhone 16 and Pro Max in landscape: tab bar (not the split view).\n\nPost the results (screenshots plus pass/fail list) on #372.\n",
