   "body": "### Update: #372 now at `fe1e8bd` (4.0.4 build 37)\nThese checks replace the « known: the topic is not carried over » expectations above.\n\n**Tests**\n```sh\nxcodebuild test -project SuperHFRplus.xcodeproj -scheme HFRswift -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 17' -only-testing:HFRswiftTests/FoldHandoffStoreTests 2>&1 | grep -E \"Test Case|error:|TEST (SUCCEEDED|FAILED)\"\n```\n\n**Fold / unfold: the topic must follow, on the same page**\n- [ ] Cover screen: Favoris → topic → go to page 3 → unfold. The split shows the same topic on page 3, with the row selected in Favoris.\n- [ ] Inner display: Catégories → forum → topic → page 5 → fold. The Catégories tab shows the topic pushed on page 5. Back returns to the categories list.\n- [ ] Close the topic on the cover screen (Back), wait 1 s, unfold: empty detail, the topic does **not** come back.\n- [ ] Inside a topic, open an internal link (a second topic stacked), then fold or unfold: the root topic is reopened (the stacked one is not, as expected).\n- [ ] Messages (MP) and Plus › Bookmarks: same round trip.\n- [ ] iPad: Split View resize regular → compact → regular with a topic open: same behaviour, no regression.\n- [ ] Console `[RootTabAudit] foldHandoff.rootSwap … reading=page N/M` on each fold.\n\n**Portrait on the inner display**\n- [ ] Choosing a topic hides the list (full-width topic). Rotating to landscape brings list + topic back. Rotating to portrait hides it again. The page being read is **not** reset by rotation.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
